{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And the flax, etc.</b> One needs to know why the verse arranged this matter before completing the matter of Moses' prayer, which he had promised: ״כְּצֵאתִי אֶת הָעִיר״ etc. He should have finished and said that Moses did so, and went out from Pharaoh and prayed etc., and afterward informed us of what the hail did." "<b>Or perhaps</b> it intends to juxtapose this matter to His saying ״טֶרֶם תִּירְאוּן אֶת HaShem״, to hint at the cause that caused them to harden their heart, and He said <b>וְהַפִּשְׁתָּה</b> etc. And they of blessed memory said in Midrash Tanchuma, and this is its language: ״כִּי אֲפִלוֹת״ — wonders of wonders were performed for them, that they were not struck; end quote. And behold, when Pharaoh saw that the plague of hail did not prevail over the wheat and the spelt contrary to nature, as they said, wonders of wonders were performed for them, he would not attribute it to HaShem having performed a wonder, but would attribute it to the thought that the dominion of the God of Israel does not extend over all that occurs — and this would imply, Heaven forbid, partnership [of other powers] and lack of universal dominion, and this would be for him grounds to harden his heart. And therefore Moses said <b>יָדַעְתִּי כִּי טֶרֶם תִּירְאוּן</b>, and its reason is <b>כִּי הַפִּשְׁתָּה</b> etc. <b>וְהַחִטָּה</b> etc. <b>לֹא נֻכּוּ</b>, and HaShem performed this wonder in order to harden Pharaoh's heart, as He had spoken: ״וַאֲנִי אֲחַזֵּק״ etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:16.167648214Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}